WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:08.670
If only... if only I hadn't gone looking for 
that ghost, this never would've happened!

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.840
Shut up!

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.510
Don't spit on Sidune's resolve.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:19.470
This time it isn't the usual free-for-all. 
Another victory condition has been given.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.140
There is a gate set up at this point.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.290
The side that reaches it first

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.150
will receive five times as many Energy Cubes
as we've been given previously.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.190
That is what the Timekeepers have told us.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.110
As for the forward members...

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.370
Please let me do it!

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.200
I want to make up for Sidune's death.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.370
I'll fight for that cause!

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.830
Then, never look back.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.710
I've got your back!

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.050
It's not like her...

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.920
She missed the vitals.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.940
There it is!

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.920
<i>Stop.</i>

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.010
<i>Continuing combat any further
will be a violation of the rules.</i>

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.640
<i>This game is already over.</i>

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.780
Come.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.660
I'll give you your reward 
for winning the game.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.120
It can't be....

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.500
Sidune?

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:25.970
Revelation: Two Histories

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.640
Are you a Timekeeper?

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.100
Yes, that's correct.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.400
But the way you look...

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:41.490
I've borrowed this image from your conscious 
mind to enable us to understand one another.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:46.200
It appears you spent the entire battle 
thinking about this individual.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:52.750
Congratulations.
This is your reward for reaching the goal.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.210
It was originally intended for one person,
but both of you arrived simultaneously.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.720
Because we reached the goal at the same time,
you're giving them to both of us.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.470
How generous of you.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.930
I didn't come here for something like this.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.690
What in the world are you Timekeepers?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:19.980
The fact that you made the effort to take that form
means you intend to tell us, right?

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:26.910
Very well. I believe you're aware of this,
 but we Timekeepers are from the future.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.530
We've come to save you.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.210
Looks like the kid made it to the goal.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.250
So do we just retreat now?

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:44.220
It'd be nice if the other side
lets us go quietly, master.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.300
Of course, that won't happen.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:53.890
Looks like there's still a job left for us.
Though, that's to be expected.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:01.070
Since defeating the other team gives us 
additional energy cubes besides those from the race,

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.900
there's no reason to hold back.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:06.740
Let's retreat. The rest is up to Tohru.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.030
All right.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.160
<i>Pull this off, Tohru.</i>

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.840
I hope you're not thinking
you can get away so easily!

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.800
And you’re gonna pay for this!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:36.560
Kyoka...

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.110
Staying here will gradually wear us down.
What should we do?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.520
We have no choice.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.570
I'll rush in and drive them out,
so cover me.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:50.950
H-Hold on! There's no way I can let
someone younger than me do that!

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.780
If anyone's going, it'll be me.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.740
But...

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:00.330
Oh, you caught me!

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.500
I guess I'll just have to fight 
you with everything I have!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.890
I've already predicted your movements!

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.690
Let us bring an end to the battle!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:29.900
Someone from the future...
So it's just like what Remy told me.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.700
From the future?

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.830
You came to save us?

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:37.330
Then why are you making us fight like this?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:41.620
Because that's the best way 
to minimize the damage.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.130
Minimize the damage?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:49.920
Ten years from their current times, both of your worlds
will successfully develop time-warp technology.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.470
Time-warp technology?
You mean the time machine?

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.350
No.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:01.070
Compared to what's to be created 10 years
from your current time,

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.020
your "time machine" is merely a toy.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.190
A toy?

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:11.990
The time-warp technology that's to be created
would even allow travel between your two worlds.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.280
But what does that time-warp tech
from 10 years in the future

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.120
have to do with making us fight?

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:24.330
With the completion of time-warp technology,
the gap between your worlds is bridged.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.000
This leads to war.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:32.220
And during that war, both of 
your worlds destroy each other.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.230
Shields activated.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.850
Shields activated.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.020
Shields activated.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:54.200
You... where'd you get that gear?

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.030
It's the power I gained to protect Tohru.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.910
You don't have it?

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:01.330
Damn you!

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:02.910
I won't let you!

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.170
Aaron!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.710
Looks like they outnumber us now...

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.260
If we get greedy, they might wipe us all out.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:14.260
You're right.  Let's split up and retreat.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:15.930
Understood. Best of luck to you.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.850
Damn you!

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.520
What? Hold on, Remy!

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.520
Kyoka! Leave that to me.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.150
I'm more used to this than you are.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:25.690
But—

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.360
You go ahead and retreat.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.650
Take care of Remy for me, okay?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.110
<i>What's the situation?</i>

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:39.580
They're retreating,
but continuing combat nonetheless.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.330
<i>Perhaps it's a warrior's instinct to fight.</i>

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:48.880
<i>It would be wonderful if we could 
decrease their number here, but...</i>

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:53.050
However, combat in a situation
different than normal is dangerous.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.330
<i>You say that,</i>

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:58.640
<i>but if there's an enemy in front of them,
they've no choice but to fight.</i>

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:02.890
<i>Anyone who isn't your ally is 
your enemy. That's how it is.</i>

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:06.060
And if shot at, people will shoot back.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:11.520
Warriors can't stop the unending cycle 
of warfare. It's a barbaric thing.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.740
<i>Barbaric?</i>

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.320
Yes. It's barbarism.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:22.540
Power must be controlled by wisdom,
but it's a difficult task.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:29.050
Why would there be war just
because we'd be able to go

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:31.000
back and forth between our worlds?

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.920
It's happened many times throughout history.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:37.260
Resources, territory, wealth...

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:41.600
Humans fight each other in order to
gain something they don't have.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:57.450
It can't be that simple...

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:58.740
It is simple.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:04.910
How can you be concerned with the lives of others
when you're about to starve to death?

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:05.870
But—

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:06.960
Exactly.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:14.710
Your worlds will fight one another, kill each other,
and, in the end, both will be destroyed.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.610
Mr. President!

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:52.920
And that future destruction
has an effect on your current selves.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.290
Effect?

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.550
What you call Degradation in your world,
the phenomenon that turns people to sand...

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:04.680
is occuring because your 
worlds don't have a future.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.980
We have no future?

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.720
The war between the two worlds

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.530
has caused the spacetime continuum
itself to become unstable.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:21.240
The degradation is a result of that.

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:50.480
Just like you pictured in your conscious mind,
everything will turn to sand and disappear.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.310
People, the world, everything.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:13:01.030
So what? Our worlds have no future, and that 
affects us in the past and turns us into sand?

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:04.410
Whether you believe it or not, it's true.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:08.080
If the situation is left unaltered, 
everything will be destroyed.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.460
However, there is still a way.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.250
There's a way?

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:20.670
There's a way to not be destroyed?

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.920
What do we need to do? Tell us!

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.140
It's not difficult.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.310
If, at this rate, both worlds
are going to be destroyed,

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:34.350
the way to fix that is to 
destroy one of them first.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:36.600
You underestimate us!

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.770
This is to avenge Kyohma!

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.110
You're the one that's underestimating us!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.490
<i>"This is to avenge Kyohma," huh?</i>

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.500
<i>So you must've been buddies
with me on the other side.</i>

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:58.210
But you know, you're the ones
that killed Sidune.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.840
I'll settle the score once and for all!

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:01.670
Big Brother!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.930
Are you all right?
We're gonna make a run for it.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:12.060
Th-Thank you so much!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:18.020
I know it's the same person, but I can't
believe I'd mistake her voice for Kyoka's...

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.070
It's useless.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.330
She's evolved her weapon with 
Energy Cubes quite a bit!

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:48.840
I won't let you get away!

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.230
Unfortunately for you,

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:05.940
I'm equipped with three sensors for sonar waves,
electromagnetic pulses, and gravitational pulses.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.950
Trying to blind me
with something like this is pointless.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.070
Why don't you give up right about now?

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.370
No way!

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:13.830
I see.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.120
All right!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:22.590
Impossible... he can fool the 
gravitational pulse sensor?

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.000
You fell for it!

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:27.050
Another dummy!

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.890
An irregularity like this...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.450
How irritating.
She just kept getting in my way.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:01.370
It was the first time I had to
deal with a weapon that was so evolved.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.290
It had tremendous firepower.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:11.050
At this rate, my psychic powers
won't be able to keep up with the enemy's evolution.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:15.220
Dammit...

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.680
One of us has to destroy the other first?

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:24.230
It makes more sense for one world 
to be destroyed than two, yes?

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:29.780
I see. And if so, who gets to decide
which world is doomed?

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.200
Is that what you Timekeepers do?

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:38.370
Indeed. We believe you 
should decide. Don't you?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.410
What do you mean?

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.000
The game we're holding right now.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:48.590
That's what these duels in 2015, between 
those capable of spacetime transfer, are for.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:53.720
Why do you make us fight in the past?
What is the significance of the year 2015?

00:16:54.720 --> 00:17:00.480
Because it's a temporal axis
that's equidistant from both of your worlds.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.100
Equidistant...

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:08.070
Yes. The year 2015 is the fairest 
battleground for both sides.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:11.190
We can't give either side an advantage.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:16.320
And only people like us are 
capable of coming here?

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.490
What happens to the losers?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:23.210
The Timekeepers will "take care" of us?

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:27.920
No, all we do is give the 
winners Energy Cubes.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:33.010
As long as they have that power, the 
winner's universe will continue to exist naturally.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:37.140
We must keep our involvement
to an absolute minimum.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:41.220
Otherwise, we couldn't
call this a fair game, could we?

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:42.600
Game...

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:47.690
Life is awarded to the winner,
and the world of the loser will be destroyed.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.440
That will be the end of this game.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:18:00.370
<i>Hurry up and get inside!
We've already started preparing for the transfer!</i>

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:05.500
You go in first!

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.420
What about the others?

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:11.710
Everyone alive has already gone back.
We're the only ones left. Let's go.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.140
All clear on our side, master!

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.470
Yeah, I'll be right over!

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:26.440
Master!

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.400
Stay back!

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.810
W-Wait a minute!

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:08.100
I know! I know!

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.070
<i>Commencing transfer.</i>

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:29.540
A game, huh?

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.630
A game, with the survival 
of our worlds on the line.

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:37.840
The winner takes all, and the loser dies.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:42.010
That's absurd! There must be some
way for us to work it out!

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.390
The future hasn't been determined yet.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:46.310
The future hasn't been determined yet.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:50.350
Maybe that's why they're so fuzzy.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.610
The future hasn't been determined yet.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:00.360
Your future is not necessarily our future!

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:02.280
And those words mean?

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:05.740
We'll decide our future.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.870
The future of war you're talking 
about, where we pillage each other...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.580
There must be a way to 
prevent it from happening!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.170
You're too naive.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:17.920
Humans can only live by stealing
what they don't have from others.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:20.470
If there's no future,
we just take the future from others.

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:22.640
Why are you so stubborn? You're me!

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.720
And you're me.
Why don't you understand?

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:37.320
What's this?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.570
What's going on?

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.240
I believe I said that
the game has concluded.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.950
But this seems like a good opportunity.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.450
Let us move the hands of time forward.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.140
W-Wait!

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.400
Work has been really hard lately.

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:29.410
At times like that, you go to the 
countryside to refresh yourself!

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:32.490
City kids have the dumbest ideas. 
There's nothing in the countryside.

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:37.160
The amusement is that there's nothing there!
You can pretend it's a world where civilization's collapsed!

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:38.400
Next episode: "Castaway"

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.920
<b><i>Castaway </i></b>The Other World

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:39.920
"The Other World"
